config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_IMP_TEST
	bool "thingino-imp-test"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_INGENIC_LIB
	select BR2_PACKAGE_INGENIC_MUSL if BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_MUSL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_INGENIC_UCLIBC if BR2_TOOLCHAIN_USES_UCLIBC
	help
	  Minimal IMP test tools:
	  - imp-test-audio: audio capture, isolated.
	  - imp-test-video: FrameSource chn0 -> encoder chn0 bring-up harness
	    (no OSD/RTSP), with a caller-stack canary and a SIGSEGV handler
	    that prints pc/ra/sp/gp. Takes an optional PollingStream timeout
	    argument (0 = non-blocking).

	  Also installs imp-test-expr: a libimp AE/exposure probe
	  (dlsym-based, no IMP link-time dependency). Reports which AE
	  APIs the running libimp exports, reads the current exposure
	  state via GetExpr, and can pin the AE integration time with
	  IMP_ISP_Tuning_SetExpr(MANUAL) (--manual-us/--manual-lines) or
	  cap it with SetAe_IT_MAX (--cap-us/--cap-lines). --watch N
	  samples whether the pinned exposure survives AE re-seizure.
	  Generation note: SetExpr exists on T10/T20/T21/T23/T30/T31-class
	  libs; T32/T40/T41-class libs use SetAeExprInfo instead (the
	  probe reports which is present).
